SUMMARY:Gentle Yoga Flow: A Beginner Yoga Class
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a calming\, beginner-friendly yoga class designed to help you unwind\, stretch\, and move with ease. This all-levels session is perfect for anyone looking to build flexibility\, reduce stress\, and explore mindful movement in a welcoming environment. With over ten years' experience\, Hannah Cherry offers supportive guidance for every body. All are welcome— no prior yoga experience needed. Please wear comfortable clothes. There are a limited amount of yoga mats available\, but patrons are welcome to bring their own.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/gentle-yoga-flow%3a-a-beginner-yoga-class/25945/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventfallfestivalatmagnoliameadowfarms17423-20260926@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261030T164000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260926
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261102
SUMMARY:Fall Festival at Magnolia Meadow Farms
DESCRIPTION:Your Fall Starts Here! Home to Maryland’s Largest Corn Maze\, we’re more than just a pumpkin patch! Located in beautiful Northern Frederick County\, just 1 hour west of Baltimore and 1.5 hours north of D.C. Come spend a day on the farm with something for everyone to enjoy! Maryland’s Largest Corn Maze with over 5 miles of trails\, PLUS: Famous Apple Cannons Hayrides to the Pumpkin Patch Farm Animal Interactions Gem Mining Mini Ziplines Jumping Pillow Mountain Slides Pedal Karts PICK-YOUR-OWN: Sunflowers Cut flowers and wildflowers Pumpkins in all shapes\, sizes\, & colors! GATHER: Share stories around a Private Campfire! Live entertainment every Saturday & Sunday! EAT: Enjoy a farm fresh meal with local beef\, pork\, and poultry! Freshly Made Apple Cider Donuts Freshly Made Kettle Corn Beer & Wine (21+\, ID required) SHOP: Pick up locally made products! Farm Fresh Honey Goat Milk Soap Baked Goods Magnolia Meadow Farms t-shirts\, sweatshirts\, & hats HOURS: September 26 - November 1 Saturdays: 10:00am to 8:00pm Sundays: 10:00am to 6:00pm Check our website for special days & hours!
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/fall-festival-at-magnolia-meadow-farms/17423/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventsummersfarmfallfestival12916-20260926@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261030T164000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260926
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261102
SUMMARY:Summers Farm Fall Festival
DESCRIPTION:Join us for our annual Fall Festival at Summers Farm! For over 30 years\, Summers Farm has been the go-to destination for fall fun in Frederick County\, Maryland. With 45+ exciting activities\, there’s something for everyone to enjoy! Whether you're planning a day of family fun\, a corporate outing\, a school field trip\, an adventurous day date\, or just some good old-fashioned fun—Summers Farm is the place to be this fall! Here's what we have planned: Pumpkin Train Photo Ops Specialty Food & Drinks Famous Corn Maze Petting Zoo Wagon Rides Pedal Car Track Giant Slides Local Food Vendors 45+ Attractions & so much more! September 26 – November 1 September Sat – Sun: 10am – 7pm October 1 – 4 Thurs – Sun: 1pm – 7pm (Thurs)\, 1pm – 9pm (Fri)\, 10am – 9pm (Sat)\, 10am – 7pm (Sun) October 7 – 31 Wed – Thurs: 1pm – 7pm Fri: 1pm – 9pm Sat: 10am – 9pm Sun: 10am – 7pm November 1 (Sunday only) 10am – 7pm *October 12\, 16 & 26th – School Daze Craze: 11:30am – 9pm
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/summers-farm-fall-festival/12916/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventpumpkinpatchatmaynes24117-20261001@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261030T164000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261001
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261101
SUMMARY:Pumpkin Patch At Mayne's
DESCRIPTION:Pumpkin Patch At Mayne's Celebrate Fall at Mayne's Tree Farm Pumpkin Patch in Frederick\, MD. Our pumpkin patch is open for the month of October on weekdays from 10a.m. - 6p.m. and on the weekends from 10a.m. - 5p.m. Pumpkins are available in small\, medium and large. Large groups by appointment during the week. Click Here for our full events schedule on facebook! Fall Activities Include: Hayrides To The Patch Corn Maze Apple Cider Scarecrow Making Straw Jumpin Antique Tractor Display For Your Fall Decoration Needs We Offer: Gourds ~ Mini Pumpkins ~ Indian Corn ~ Corn Stalks ~ Straw Bales
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/pumpkin-patch-at-maynes/24117/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventlegends26lore26224-20261009@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261030T164000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261009
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261031
SUMMARY:Legends & Lore
DESCRIPTION:Come see the darker side of Frederick. When night falls\, Frederick’s familiar streets have rather different stories to tell. Climb aboard our vintage double-decker for an hour of dark tales from Frederick’s past\, researched from local histories\, old accounts and the legends that have lingered long after the people involved have gone. As we make our way through the city\, we’ll slow down at the very places connected to these stories\, from historic streets and old buildings to some of Frederick’s more famously haunted places. Along the way\, you’ll hear tales of strange happenings\, restless spirits and the darker chapters of local history\, all told against the backdrop of Frederick after dark. And because it’s October\, you’ll also get a rather good view from the top deck as the city’s historic homes and neighborhoods put on their best autumn and Halloween displays. Whether you’re a believer\, a skeptic\, or simply enjoy a good story with a slightly unsettling ending\, Legends and Lore offers a different way to discover Frederick’s history. Just remember\, it’s much easier to laugh at a ghost story when you’re not sitting on the top deck in the dark. TOUR HIGHLIGHTS Hear researched tales of Frederick’s haunted places\, local legends and darker history\, told where the stories happened. Experience Frederick after dark from the top deck\, with historic streets\, autumn displays and a few places you’ll look at rather differently afterwards. TOUR DETAILS Price: $35 per person Duration: 1 hour Recommended Age: 14+ Departure: RAK Brewing Co\, 400 Sagner Ave\, Frederick\, MD\, 21701
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/legends-%26-lore/26224/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventtrailofjackolanternswithtrickortreating9284-20261016@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261030T164000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261016
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261101
SUMMARY:Trail of Jack-O-Lanterns with Trick or Treating
DESCRIPTION:Looking for something fun to do with the children this October that won’t scare them and is appropriate for any age? You found it! Join us 6pm to 10pm for our walking Trail of Jack-O-Lanterns. Admission is $16.00\, credit only ages 2 and older (babies are free) & includes our Trail\, fire pits\, and our Animal Barn (open 6pm to 9:00pm.) to see your furry friends. Admission will also include trick or treating for children from 7pm to 8pm. The Trail closes at 9pm. Bring your children (and your adults) in costume to add to the fun! Available for purchase will be night hayrides\, pumpkin flashlights\, Trick or Treat bags\, glow necklaces\, and more! Gates open 5:30pm. Last admission is 8:30pm. Check our website for NEW nightly specials! Dates: Oct 16\, 17\, 18\, 23\, 24\, 25\, 30 and 31\, 2026 (weather permitting) NOTE: The Trail is a separate event from our daytime petting farm and requires a separate\, new admission to enter.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/trail-of-jack-o-lanterns-with-trick-or-treating/9284/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventtrekortreat21019-20261016@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261030T164000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261016
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261101
SUMMARY:Trek or Treat
DESCRIPTION:Get off the screen and into the scream at Tree Trekkers for Trek or Treat! It’s trick or treat in the trees! This Halloween\, the forest transforms into a treetop adventure full of tricks\, treats\, and thrills. Climb\, zip\, and creep your way through the trails as candy stations await in the canopy. Bigfoot’s lurking in the woods… but don’t worry\, he’s just here for the candy! Landing zones are sponsored by our favorite local businesses with treats that will delight not fright! Costumes encouraged! (Make sure we can still harness you though!) Prizes for best dressed trekkers! A spooktacular adventure for all ages 4+ (4 -7 year olds will need to climb with an adult) Trek or Treat bag is included with Trek or Treat Ticket. $7 Trek or Treat add on bags available for Little-foot combo tickets\, gift voucher redemptions\, and groups. (Call to book 301-888-8735) Trek or Treat bags can also be purchased for younger siblings who want to trick or treat on our ground pathway sponsored by our local non-profits. Includes access to all 16 Timber Trek Trails Climbers will begin their adventure in ground school\, advancing to the bunny slope trails where they will need to show competency with their equipment and a firm understanding of the course rules before advancing to the main platform. Gloves are highly recommended\, but not required. Guests can bring their own full-finger climbing gloves or purchase gloves if they choose. This is a self guided adventure recommended for ages 8+ (4-7 year olds require an adult climber to climb with them and will be required to start on our purple trails) Participants will need to be 4ft or taller to go on our Red Zipline Trails Weight Limit: 30-250lbs Everyone on the property will need to sign a waiver. (This includes climbers and spectators) Must wear closed toed/closed heeled shoes\, such as sneakers or boots\, no crocs\, sandals\, or backless footwear. If you do not see a time or date available that works with your schedule please call 301-888-8735 or email INFO@TREETREKKERSMD.COM TREK OR TREAT DATES: 10/16\, 10/17\, 10/23\, 10/24\, 10/30\, 10/31 (ONLY TREK OR TREAT TICKETS ARE AVAILABLE ON THOSE DATES) TREK OR TREAT
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/trek-or-treat/21019/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventfredericksblackheritagewalkingtour23752-20261017@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261030T164000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261017
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261101
SUMMARY:Frederick's Black Heritage Walking Tour
DESCRIPTION:Visit landmarks and hear stories revealing Frederick’s Black heritage from the early-19th century to the present day. This tour features sites associated with enslavement and segregation and highlights the achievements of a diverse and vibrant Black community in the pursuit of equality and freedom. *Tour starts at the Museum of Frederick County History\, 24 East Church Street\, Frederick\, MD 21701 Length: 90 minutes
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/fredericks-black-heritage-walking-tour/23752/
END:VEVENT
