DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261031
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261101
SUMMARY:Celebrate Halloween at JoJo's with Crash the Limo
DESCRIPTION:Killer costumes. Live music. A Halloween party worth crashing! Crash the Limo is taking over the Delirium Stage for a night of sing-along favorites\, wicked fun\, and Halloween mayhem at JoJo’s! Dress to impress—or frighten! The band will judge our costume contest for the sexiest\, funniest\, and scariest looks\, with JoJo’s gift cards\, JoJo’s swag\, band swag\, and treats up for grabs. Grab your crew\, fuel up with great food and drinks\, and come “Crash” the party. No cover!
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/celebrate-halloween-at-jojos-with-crash-the-limo/26282/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventechoesinthegallery3asharingspiritencounters26spiritinspiredpoetry26316-20261031@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261030T164000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261031
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261101
SUMMARY:Echoes in the Gallery: Sharing Spirit Encounters & Spirit Inspired Poetry
DESCRIPTION:An evening of intimate storytelling and remembrance. Share your personal encounters with spirits\, your beloved departed\, or the unseen. Or read poetry that bridges the living and the departed. It's not necessary to participate. We are happy to have your presence. Contact Kim to sign up or just show up. You're also welcome to visit the gallery anytime and add a photo/small offering of your departed relative or crossed-over pet to our community Ofrenda altar. It is currently set up in the gallery to celebrate Dia de Los Muertos and All Souls' Day\, which starts on the eve of Oct. 31st. Dress is casual. The gallery will serve snacks\, wine\, and beverages. Those interested in sharing an encounter or poem are encouraged to contact Kim Yourick at kim@lockhousegallery.com or call 301-969-6676 to sign up. Our gallery hours are Thursday - Sat 10-7 and Sun 10-5 if you would like to come add to the Ofrenda. History of the Ofrenda (altar): An ofrenda (altar) during Día de los Muertos (Day of the Dead) is a sacred\, temporary home or community table built to welcome and honor deceased family members and loved ones as their spirits return to visit the living on November 1 and 2. Rather than a place of mourning\, the ofrenda is a joyful celebration of memory\, identity\, and continuing love. Key Elements of the Ofrenda and Their Meanings Every item placed on the ofrenda serves a specific purpose to guide\, welcome\, or honor the returning spirits: -Photographs & Personal Items: Pictures of the deceased go on the upper tiers so the spirit feels recognized\, welcomed\, and personally remembered. You may also include favorite toys\, tools\, or clothing. Marigolds ( Cempasúchil ): The bright orange and yellow \\
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/echoes-in-the-gallery%3a-sharing-spirit-encounters-%26-spirit-inspired-poetry/26316/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventfieldfreshfarmersmarket23988-20261031@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261030T164000Z
